Subject: winex11: preserve smooth touchpad scrolling

XInput2 2.1 reports touchpad and high-resolution wheel scrolling as
cumulative valuator positions with an increment that represents one wheel
notch. Wine only consumes the legacy button events the X server synthesizes
from those valuators, reducing every update to a whole WHEEL_DELTA and making
two-finger navigation visibly stepped.

Select XI_Motion, XI_ButtonPress, and XI_ButtonRelease on each Wine window.
Preserve native scroll-valuator changes as fractional vertical and horizontal
Win32 wheel input, carrying sub-unit remainders between reports. Ignore the
corresponding emulated XI scroll-button duplicate so each movement is delivered
once, while still accepting native XI wheel buttons from devices without
scroll axes.

Selecting a master-device XI event prevents the X server from delivering its
core equivalent. Forward non-scroll XI motion and button press/release events
through Wine's existing core handlers, including button state reconstruction,
so the smooth path preserves ordinary pointer motion, left/right/middle clicks,
extra buttons, activation timestamps, and middle-drag handling.

The first valuator report establishes its cumulative baseline, device changes
refresh the axis metadata, and individual reports are capped at 16 notches to
avoid a discontinuity producing an extreme jump. WINE_X11_SMOOTH_SCROLL=off
restores Wine's core button path. Builds without XInput2 2.1 scroll definitions
compile this path out.

---
 dlls/winex11.drv/mouse.c  | 255 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv.h |  16 +++
 2 files changed, 271 insertions(+)

